window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Algebraic Geometry", "projects": [{"id": "AG-01", "slug": "hilbert-basis-theorem", "title": "Hilbert Basis Theorem and Affine Finiteness", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>Collect possible coefficients at each degree into an ascending chain\nof ideals. Once that chain stabilizes, finitely many chosen polynomials\nreduce every other polynomial by decreasing degree.</p>", "target": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a commutative Noetherian ring with identity (every ideal is finitely\ngenerated), then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Noetherian. Deduce by induction that every ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis finitely generated for a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso every affine algebraic set is cut out by finitely many polynomial\nequations.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use elementary ideal arithmetic and polynomial coefficients,\nincluding degree reduction by cancellation of a leading coefficient.\nNoetherianity implies the ascending chain condition: the union of an\nascending chain is an ideal; its finitely many generators all lie in one\nterm, which therefore equals the union. For an ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>\ndenotes its common zero set over the chosen field. No algebraic closure\nhypothesis is needed here.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Coefficient ideals stabilize", "role": "<p>Encode infinitely many polynomial constraints in an ascending chain\ninside the Noetherian coefficient ring. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong> There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d=A_N</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\ge N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finitely many chosen polynomial lifts in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>An ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">coefficient of </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> in </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">deg</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d=\\{\\text{coefficient of }x^d\\text{ in }f:f\\in I,\\deg f\\le d\\}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nincluding zero.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d=A_N</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\ge N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finitely many chosen polynomial lifts in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Use coefficient ideals at degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>;\na set of leading coefficients at exactly one degree requires care under\ncancellation.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a sum cancels leading coefficients, retain the\ncoefficient-at-degree definition, which includes zero and remains an\nideal. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials of degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>\nshow that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplication by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nshows\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d\\subset A_{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe ascending chain condition gives stabilization at some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le d\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{d,1},\\ldots,a_{d,r_d}</annotation></semantics></math>\nof\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOmit zero generators. Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{d,j}\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nof degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhose coefficient at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^d</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA nonzero chosen coefficient makes its degree exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThere are only finitely many chosen polynomials.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d=A_N</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\ge N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finitely many chosen polynomial lifts in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>An ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">coefficient of </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> in </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">deg</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d=\\{\\text{coefficient of }x^d\\text{ in }f:f\\in I,\\deg f\\le d\\}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nincluding zero. Retain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Encode infinitely many polynomial constraints in an ascending chain\ninside the Noetherian coefficient ring.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Use coefficient ideals at degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>;\na set of leading coefficients at exactly one degree requires care under\ncancellation.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Degree descent generates the ideal", "role": "<p>Cancel the highest coefficient of an arbitrary polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand use induction on its degree. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Noetherian.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\ngenerated in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nby the finite chosen family. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Noetherian.</p>", "gate": "<p>The degree must strictly decrease after cancellation, even when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas zero divisors.</p>", "repair": "<p>If polynomial long division over a field is used for a general ring,\nreplace it by the generator combination above; invertibility is not\nassumed. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Certainly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J\\subset I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nLet nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave degree\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nand leading coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\min(m,N)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nStabilization gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in A_m=A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand membership is immediate when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=\\sum_j b_j a_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_j\\in R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=f-\\sum_j b_j x^{m-d}f_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has degree less than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nor is zero. Strong induction on the nonnegative integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nproves\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAt\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncancellation leaves zero, which starts the induction. No division by a\nleading coefficient was used.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Noetherian.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\ngenerated in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nby the finite chosen family. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Cancel the highest coefficient of an arbitrary polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand use induction on its degree.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The degree must strictly decrease after cancellation, even when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas zero divisors.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Finite equations in affine space", "role": "<p>Iterate the one-variable theorem and translate ideal generation into\nequality of zero sets. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finite generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_1,\\ldots,g_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)=V(g_1,\\ldots,g_s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E2/v1 and a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose only ideals are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finite generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_1,\\ldots,g_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)=V(g_1,\\ldots,g_s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Equality of zero sets follows from linear combinations of equations,\nnot from radical-ideal correspondence.</p>", "repair": "<p>If finite generation is claimed for infinitely many variables,\nrestore the finite-variable contract before reusing the induction.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>A field is Noetherian. Apply E2 successively to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand so on to obtain Noetherianity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe induction length is the finite number of variables.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(g_1,\\ldots,g_s)</annotation></semantics></math>,\na point annihilating all generators annihilates each finite polynomial\ncombination of them, hence all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe reverse implication is immediate because the generators belong to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the finite-equation conclusion.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas finite generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_1,\\ldots,g_s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)=V(g_1,\\ldots,g_s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E2/v1 and a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose only ideals are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Iterate the one-variable theorem and translate ideal generation into\nequality of zero sets.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Equality of zero sets follows from linear combinations of equations,\nnot from radical-ideal correspondence.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\ngenerated in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nby the finite chosen family. Check: The degree must strictly decrease\nafter cancellation, even when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas zero divisors.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E2/v1 and a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose only ideals are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: Equality of zero sets follows from linear combinations of\nequations, not from radical-ideal correspondence.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-coefficient-ideals-stabilize-1\">N1 — Coefficient ideals\nstabilize</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Addition and scalar multiplication of\npolynomials of degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>\nshow that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplication by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nshows\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d\\subset A_{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe ascending chain condition gives stabilization at some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le d\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose generators\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{d,1},\\ldots,a_{d,r_d}</annotation></semantics></math>\nof\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOmit zero generators. Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{d,j}\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nof degree at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhose coefficient at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^d</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA nonzero chosen coefficient makes its degree exactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThere are only finitely many chosen polynomials.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-degree-descent-generates-the-ideal-1\">N2 — Degree descent\ngenerates the ideal</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Certainly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J\\subset I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nLet nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave degree\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nand leading coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\min(m,N)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nStabilization gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in A_m=A_d</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand membership is immediate when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\le N</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWrite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=\\sum_j b_j a_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b_j\\in R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> The polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=f-\\sum_j b_j x^{m-d}f_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has degree less than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nor is zero. Strong induction on the nonnegative integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>\nproves\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAt\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncancellation leaves zero, which starts the induction. No division by a\nleading coefficient was used.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-finite-equations-in-affine-space-1\">N3 — Finite equations in\naffine space</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> A field is Noetherian. Apply E2\nsuccessively to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand so on to obtain Noetherianity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe induction length is the finite number of variables.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(g_1,\\ldots,g_s)</annotation></semantics></math>,\na point annihilating all generators annihilates each finite polynomial\ncombination of them, hence all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe reverse implication is immediate because the generators belong to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the finite-equation conclusion.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x,y]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe generated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^2,xy,xy^2,xy^3,\\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xy^m=y^{m-1}(xy)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(x^2,xy)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts common zeros satisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>-axis.\nFinite generation does not say\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis radical:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes on that axis but\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\notin I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>The ring\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,x_2,\\ldots]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not Noetherian. If the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x_1,x_2,\\ldots)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhad finitely many generators, they would involve only finitely many\nvariables. Setting those variables to zero would annihilate every\nproposed generator but leave a later variable nonzero, contradicting\ngeneration.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 activity:</strong> divide by the leading\ncoefficient of a polynomial over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb Z[x]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe coefficient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>\nneed not be invertible. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Intellect\nsubstituted a field division algorithm for a ring argument.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> express the leading coefficient in the ideal\ngenerated by the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_{d,j}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand subtract the corresponding polynomial combination. The degree falls\nwithout division; recheck E2 and the affine consequence. The theorem\nremains unchanged.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use finite polynomial descriptions as input to\nelimination and local computations; finite generation alone gives no\npractical degree bound.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/ag.html\">J. S.\nMilne, Algebraic Geometry</a>, chapters on commutative algebra,\nalgebraic sets, and affine varieties; <a\nhref=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/\">author’s mathematics site</a>.</p>", "sha256": "1b200123527bd1aefad124568f0e39a051a92c4ab26c033773fff3c49809f2e9", "pdf": "reports/pdf/hilbert-basis-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "AG-02", "slug": "weak-nullstellensatz", "title": "Weak Nullstellensatz", "level": "Advanced", "idea": "<p>A field that is finitely generated as a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\ncannot contain a transcendental generator: integrality would force a\npolynomial ring with only one denominator inverted to be a field.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe algebraically closed and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith finite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery maximal ideal is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x_1-a_1,\\ldots,x_n-a_n)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a unique point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in k^n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConsequently every proper ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a common zero in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use existence of maximal ideals containing proper ideals (Zorn’s\nlemma), finite transcendence bases chosen from a finite generating set,\nand elementary field algebra. Import the integrality facts: finitely\nmany integral elements generate a finite module; every element of a\nfinite-module algebra is integral, by the determinant trick. An element\nis integral over a ring if it satisfies a monic polynomial with\ncoefficients in that ring. The finite-generation field lemma needed\nbelow is proved here, not imported as the target.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Clear algebraic denominators", "role": "<p>Separate a maximal algebraically independent subset and make the\nremaining generators integral after one localization. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong> For algebraically independent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1,\\ldots,t_r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthere is nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\in k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r]</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,1/d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k[b_1,\\ldots,b_m]</annotation></semantics></math>\nover the algebraically closed field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>For algebraically independent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1,\\ldots,t_r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthere is nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\in k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r]</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,1/d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Finite generation is as an algebra, not merely as a field; only\nfinitely many denominators need to be inverted.</p>", "repair": "<p>If arbitrary rational coefficients are treated as polynomial\ncoefficients, explicitly collect their finitely many denominators into\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Choose a maximal algebraically independent subset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1,\\ldots,t_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nof the generators. Every remaining generator\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis algebraic over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=k(t_1,\\ldots,t_r)</annotation></semantics></math>:\notherwise the subset could be enlarged. Each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfies a monic polynomial over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the product of the finitely many polynomial denominators in these\nmonic equations (take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nif there are none). The\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,1/d]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a field,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/d\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>;\nbecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,u_1,\\ldots,u_s]</annotation></semantics></math>\nas an algebra,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B[u_1,\\ldots,u_s]=K</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe stated integrality facts now show\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For\nalgebraically independent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1,\\ldots,t_r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthere is nonzero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\in k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r]</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,1/d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>A field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k[b_1,\\ldots,b_m]</annotation></semantics></math>\nover the algebraically closed field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Separate a maximal algebraically independent subset and make the\nremaining generators integral after one localization.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Finite generation is as an algebra, not merely as a field; only\nfinitely many denominators need to be inverted.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Eliminate transcendence", "role": "<p>First force\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nto be a field, then find a polynomial that cannot become a unit in that\nlocalization. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every finitely generated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nthat is a field.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\na field integral over the domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every finitely generated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nthat is a field.</p>", "gate": "<p>The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis infinite; choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>\nso that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\ndoes not divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the localization is declared a field without proof, derive\ninverses from monic equations; if transcendence is ignored, use the\nnonunit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\nwitness. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\ne b\\in B</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe element\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{-1}\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(b^{-1})^q+c_{q-1}(b^{-1})^{q-1}+\\cdots+c_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplying by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{q-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexpresses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nas an element of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a field.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\in k</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c\\nmid d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSuch a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists because a nonzero polynomial has only finitely many distinct\nfactors\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhereas an algebraically closed field is infinite. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\nwere invertible in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(t_1-c)q=d^s</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSubstituting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1=c</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives a contradiction since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(c,t_2,\\ldots,t_r)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould not be a field. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>All generators are now algebraic over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand finitely many algebraic generators give a finite algebraic\nextension. Algebraic closedness implies that extension is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nitself. This proves the required finite-generation field lemma for this\nbase field.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every finitely generated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nthat is a field.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\na field integral over the domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>First force\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nto be a field, then find a polynomial that cannot become a unit in that\nlocalization.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis infinite; choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>\nso that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\ndoes not divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Recover the affine point", "role": "<p>Identify each coordinate residue with a scalar and identify the\nkernel of evaluation. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> Maximal ideals\nare exactly point ideals, and every proper ideal has a common zero.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A maximal ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔪</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak m\\subset A</annotation></semantics></math>\nand E2/v1 applied to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=A/\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>Maximal ideals are exactly point ideals, and every proper ideal has a\ncommon zero.</p>", "gate": "<p>The quotient is a field because the ideal is maximal; the scalar\nidentification must respect the given embedding of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a nonmaximal ideal is treated as having a field quotient, first\npass to a maximal ideal containing it. Withhold this export and recheck\nits descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A/\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>\nis generated as a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nby the coordinate residues. E2 identifies it with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nas a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra.\nWrite the residue of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i-a_i\\in\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Evaluation at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x_1-a_1,\\ldots,x_n-a_n)</annotation></semantics></math>:\nrepeatedly replace coordinates by their values, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)-f(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a sum of multiples of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i-a_i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThat point ideal is maximal, since evaluation has quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand inclusion forces equality with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔪</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nUniqueness follows by comparing coordinate values.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis proper, place it inside a maximal ideal and use its point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe only proper ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis zero, and the unique empty coordinate tuple gives the same\nstatement.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: Maximal ideals\nare exactly point ideals, and every proper ideal has a common zero.</p>", "Memory": "<p>A maximal ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔪</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak m\\subset A</annotation></semantics></math>\nand E2/v1 applied to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=A/\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Identify each coordinate residue with a scalar and identify the\nkernel of evaluation.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The quotient is a field because the ideal is maximal; the scalar\nidentification must respect the given embedding of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\na field integral over the domain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis infinite; choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>\nso that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\ndoes not divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>A maximal ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔪</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak m\\subset A</annotation></semantics></math>\nand E2/v1 applied to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=A/\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The quotient is a field because the ideal is maximal; the scalar\nidentification must respect the given embedding of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-clear-algebraic-denominators-1\">N1 — Clear algebraic\ndenominators</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Choose a maximal algebraically independent\nsubset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1,\\ldots,t_r</annotation></semantics></math>\nof the generators. Every remaining generator\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nis algebraic over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=k(t_1,\\ldots,t_r)</annotation></semantics></math>:\notherwise the subset could be enlarged. Each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfies a monic polynomial over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the product of the finitely many polynomial denominators in these\nmonic equations (take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nif there are none). The\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nare integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,1/d]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a field,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/d\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>;\nbecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=k[t_1,\\ldots,t_r,u_1,\\ldots,u_s]</annotation></semantics></math>\nas an algebra,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B[u_1,\\ldots,u_s]=K</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe stated integrality facts now show\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-eliminate-transcendence-1\">N2 — Eliminate transcendence</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\ne b\\in B</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe element\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{-1}\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>\nis integral:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(b^{-1})^q+c_{q-1}(b^{-1})^{q-1}+\\cdots+c_0=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplying by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{q-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexpresses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nas an element of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a field.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\in k</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c\\nmid d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSuch a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists because a nonzero polynomial has only finitely many distinct\nfactors\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhereas an algebraically closed field is infinite. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1-c</annotation></semantics></math>\nwere invertible in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(t_1-c)q=d^s</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand integer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSubstituting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t_1=c</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives a contradiction since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(c,t_2,\\ldots,t_r)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould not be a field. Therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.3.</strong> All generators are now algebraic over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand finitely many algebraic generators give a finite algebraic\nextension. Algebraic closedness implies that extension is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nitself. This proves the required finite-generation field lemma for this\nbase field.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-recover-the-affine-point-1\">N3 — Recover the affine\npoint</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A/\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>\nis generated as a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nby the coordinate residues. E2 identifies it with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nas a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra.\nWrite the residue of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i-a_i\\in\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> Evaluation at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x_1-a_1,\\ldots,x_n-a_n)</annotation></semantics></math>:\nrepeatedly replace coordinates by their values, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)-f(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a sum of multiples of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_i-a_i</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThat point ideal is maximal, since evaluation has quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand inclusion forces equality with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝔪</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nUniqueness follows by comparing coordinate values.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.3.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis proper, place it inside a maximal ideal and use its point\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery polynomial in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe only proper ideal of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nis zero, and the unique empty coordinate tuple gives the same\nstatement.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(x^2+1,y-x)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe points\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,i)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-i,-i)</annotation></semantics></math>\nboth annihilate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA maximal ideal above\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\ncan be\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x-i,y-i)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe theorem guarantees a point for each maximal ideal, not uniqueness of\nthe common zero of an arbitrary proper ideal.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x^2+1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis maximal but has no real zero. Its quotient is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\na proper finite algebraic extension of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis pinpoints the algebraic-closure assumption.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 claim:</strong> a field finitely generated as a\nfield extension must be algebraic. The field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k(t)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis generated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nas a field and is transcendental. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Memory\nconfused field generation with algebra generation.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> use the actual quotient presentation as a\nfinitely generated algebra in N1; it is precisely what yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=B[u_1,\\ldots,u_s]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNo change to the theorem is needed. Recheck E1, E2, and the\nmaximal-ideal identification.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use the maximal-ideal result in AG-03 to recover the\nfull vanishing ideal by the Rabinowitsch construction.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/ag.html\">J. S.\nMilne, Algebraic Geometry</a>, chapters on commutative algebra,\nalgebraic sets, and affine varieties; <a\nhref=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/\">author’s mathematics site</a>.</p>", "sha256": "1d3968c1008100c9f5073ac393e9a0587fadd0c092696983fbb241ba22713762", "pdf": "reports/pdf/weak-nullstellensatz.pdf"}, {"id": "AG-03", "slug": "strong-nullstellensatz", "title": "Strong Nullstellensatz via Rabinowitsch’s Trick", "level": "Advanced", "idea": "<p>Turn the assertion that a polynomial never becomes nonzero on the\nvariety into an inconsistent system by adjoining an inverse\nvariable.</p>", "target": "<p>For an algebraically closed field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nfinite\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand any ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(S)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the ideal of polynomials vanishing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> for some integer </mtext><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt I=\\{f:f^m\\in I\\text{ for some integer }m\\ge1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import AG-02 in the following exact form: a proper ideal in a\nfinite-variable polynomial ring over algebraically closed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a common zero. Use localization at the powers of a nonzero\npolynomial and finite ideal-combination identities. No effective bound\non the exponent is assumed or concluded.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Build an inconsistent enlarged system", "role": "<p>Combine vanishing of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\non the original zeros with the equation that would make it invertible.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=\\sum_{j=1}^s A_j(x,y)g_j(x)+B(x,y)(1-yf(x))</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_j\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I(V(I))</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J=(I,1-yf)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n,y]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=\\sum_{j=1}^s A_j(x,y)g_j(x)+B(x,y)(1-yf(x))</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_j\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The new variable\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nis independent; the weak Nullstellensatz applies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>\nvariables over the same algebraically closed field.</p>", "repair": "<p>If inconsistency is equated with the unit ideal over an arbitrary\nfield, restore the algebraic-closure hypothesis before invoking AG-02.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>A common zero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nof\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould satisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile also\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-bf(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis would give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas no common zero.</p>", "<p>By the contrapositive of AG-02,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the whole ring. Membership of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the generated ideal means exactly a finite polynomial-combination\nidentity of the displayed form; finite generation of all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not required for this individual identity.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\in J</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=\\sum_{j=1}^s A_j(x,y)g_j(x)+B(x,y)(1-yf(x))</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_j\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I(V(I))</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J=(I,1-yf)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n,y]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Combine vanishing of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\non the original zeros with the equation that would make it\ninvertible.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The new variable\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nis independent; the weak Nullstellensatz applies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>\nvariables over the same algebraically closed field.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Clear denominators and close both inclusions", "role": "<p>Substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmultiply by a sufficiently large power of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand prove the converse directly. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the localization step, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ntreated separately. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Zero cannot be inverted, and the exponent clearing all denominators\nmust be chosen for the finite entire sum.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the conclusion is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nrather than\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>,\nretain the denominator-clearing exponent; discarding it loses\nmultiplicity information. Withhold this export and recheck its\ndescendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit is already in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOtherwise evaluate the E1 identity in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n,1/f]</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=1/f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe last term vanishes, leaving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=\\sum_j A_j(x,1/f)g_j(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>\nat least the largest\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>-degree\nof the finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplication by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m=\\sum_j h_j(x)g_j(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely, if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)^m=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves both inclusions, including\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nequal to the unit ideal.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the localization step, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ntreated separately. Incoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the\nstated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Substitute\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmultiply by a sufficiently large power of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand prove the converse directly.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Zero cannot be inverted, and the exponent clearing all denominators\nmust be chosen for the finite entire sum.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the localization step, with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ntreated separately. Check: Zero cannot be inverted, and the exponent\nclearing all denominators must be chosen for the finite entire sum.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-build-an-inconsistent-enlarged-system-1\">N1 — Build an\ninconsistent enlarged system</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> A common zero\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nof\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould satisfy\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile also\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-bf(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis would give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas no common zero.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> By the contrapositive of AG-02,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the whole ring. Membership of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the generated ideal means exactly a finite polynomial-combination\nidentity of the displayed form; finite generation of all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not required for this individual identity.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-clear-denominators-and-close-both-inclusions-1\">N2 — Clear\ndenominators and close both inclusions</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit is already in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOtherwise evaluate the E1 identity in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n,1/f]</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=1/f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe last term vanishes, leaving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=\\sum_j A_j(x,1/f)g_j(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>\nat least the largest\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>-degree\nof the finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_j</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMultiplication by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m=\\sum_j h_j(x)g_j(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely, if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)^m=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves both inclusions, including\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>\nequal to the unit ideal.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(x^2,y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C[x,y]</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)=\\{(0,0)\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbut\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^2\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe enlarged identity for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=x</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1=(1+tx)(1-tx)+t^2x^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nillustrating exactly how substitution\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=1/x</annotation></semantics></math>\nrecovers the square.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=(x^2+1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas empty real zero set, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(V(I))=\\mathbb R[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt I=I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOver an algebraically closed field the theorem concerns radicals, not\nequality with arbitrary nonradical ideals.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 export:</strong> every polynomial vanishing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I)</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelongs to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe worked example\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\notin(x^2,y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nrefutes it. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Action discarded the power\nintroduced when clearing denominators. <strong>Repair:</strong> export\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^m\\in I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msqrt><mi>I</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in\\sqrt I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis narrows the rejected overclaim to the theorem actually stated in\n§1; the proof there already includes the correct exponent.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Deduce the inclusion-reversing correspondence\nbetween affine algebraic sets and radical ideals; then compare reduced\ncoordinate rings with nonreduced schemes.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/ag.html\">J. S.\nMilne, Algebraic Geometry</a>, chapters on commutative algebra,\nalgebraic sets, and affine varieties; <a\nhref=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/\">author’s mathematics site</a>.</p>", "sha256": "63fd04fdad3011747e043fd3b8a456b6dd1dd77458a07d46951bc139eb9019e0", "pdf": "reports/pdf/strong-nullstellensatz.pdf"}, {"id": "AG-04", "slug": "irreducibility-and-prime-ideals", "title": "Irreducibility, Prime Ideals, and Coordinate Domains", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>A product vanishes at each point exactly when at least one factor\ndoes. This translates a geometric split into zero divisors in the\ncoordinate ring.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\subset k^n</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a nonempty affine algebraic set over a field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWith its Zariski subspace topology,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible if and only if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime, equivalently the coordinate ring\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]=k[x_1,\\ldots,x_n]/I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an integral domain. Irreducible means not a union of two proper\nclosed subsets. Algebraic closedness is not needed for this statement\nabout the actual point set and its vanishing ideal.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∪</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(fg)=V(f)\\cup V(g)</annotation></semantics></math>\nover a field, the definition of the Zariski topology, and the quotient\ncriterion: a proper ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime iff\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ab\\in P</annotation></semantics></math>\nimplies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in P</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b\\in P</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe quotient is a domain precisely when this implication holds. Relative\nclosed sets in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\cap V(S)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor collections\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math>\nof polynomials.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Irreducibility forbids zero divisors", "role": "<p>Convert a vanishing product into a two-set closed cover.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Nonempty irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime.</p>", "gate": "<p>Nonemptiness makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nproper; the empty set has the unit vanishing ideal.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the empty set is included as irreducible, restore nonemptiness\nbefore claiming a proper prime ideal. Withhold this export and recheck\nits descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Nonemptiness gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\notin I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,\neach point of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(f)</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(g)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbecause a field has no zero divisors. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∪</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=(X\\cap V(f))\\cup(X\\cap V(g))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Both pieces are closed in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIrreducibility forces one to equal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves primality.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Nonempty irreducible\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Convert a vanishing product into a two-set closed cover.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Nonemptiness makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nproper; the empty set has the unit vanishing ideal.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "A closed split produces zero divisors", "role": "<p>Choose one polynomial detecting a point outside each closed subset\nand multiply them. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible, and both conditions are equivalent to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbeing a domain.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Prime\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a proposed decomposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=Y\\cup Z</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto two proper relatively closed subsets.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible, and both conditions are equivalent to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbeing a domain.</p>", "gate": "<p>A proper closed subset has a defining equation that fails somewhere\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>;\ndo not assume one equation defines the whole subset.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a single defining equation for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nis assumed without justification, select just one member of its defining\nfamily that fails at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y=X\\cap V(S)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in X\\setminus Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSome\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in S</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut is not in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSimilarly choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut not on all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The product\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y\\cup Z=X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile neither factor belongs to it, contradicting primality. Thus a\nproper split is impossible. Finally, multiplication of residue classes\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis zero exactly when the product of representatives lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe prime-ideal condition is exactly absence of nonzero zero divisors,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis prime then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible, and both conditions are equivalent to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbeing a domain.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Prime\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a proposed decomposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=Y\\cup Z</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto two proper relatively closed subsets. Retain the stated assumptions\nand import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Choose one polynomial detecting a point outside each closed subset\nand multiply them.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A proper closed subset has a defining equation that fails somewhere\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>;\ndo not assume one equation defines the whole subset.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-irreducibility-forbids-zero-divisors-1\">N1 — Irreducibility\nforbids zero divisors</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Nonemptiness gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∉</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\notin I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,\neach point of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(f)</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(g)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbecause a field has no zero divisors. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∪</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=(X\\cap V(f))\\cup(X\\cap V(g))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Both pieces are closed in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIrreducibility forces one to equal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves primality.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-a-closed-split-produces-zero-divisors-1\">N2 — A closed split\nproduces zero divisors</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y=X\\cap V(S)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in X\\setminus Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSome\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in S</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut is not in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSimilarly choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishing on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut not on all of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> The product\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y\\cup Z=X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">fg\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile neither factor belongs to it, contradicting primality. Thus a\nproper split is impossible. Finally, multiplication of residue classes\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis zero exactly when the product of representatives lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe prime-ideal condition is exactly absence of nonzero zero divisors,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=V(xy)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis the union of the two coordinate axes. The classes of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nare nonzero functions on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbut their product is zero. For the parabola\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y=V(y-x^2)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nevaluation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\mapsto t</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\mapsto t^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nidentifies its coordinate ring with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C[t]</annotation></semantics></math>:\ndivision by the monic polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y-x^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nleaves a remainder in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich vanishes at every complex\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nonly if zero. Thus the parabola is irreducible.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Connectedness is weaker than irreducibility. The two complex\ncoordinate axes meet at the origin, so their union is connected in the\nusual topology, yet the two proper algebraic axes split it. Algebraic\nirreducibility is the condition proved here.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 inference:</strong> every proper closed subset is\na hypersurface. For example the origin in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nrequires the simultaneous equations\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nas a set of two independent coordinate restrictions.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> select one defining polynomial nonzero at a\nchosen outside point; the argument needs a separator, not a single\nequation for the entire subset. This corrects the proof mechanism\nwithout changing the target. Recheck the product witness and domain\nconclusion.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use domain coordinate rings to define function\nfields of irreducible affine varieties.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/ag.html\">J. S.\nMilne, Algebraic Geometry</a>, chapters on commutative algebra,\nalgebraic sets, and affine varieties; <a\nhref=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/\">author’s mathematics site</a>.</p>", "sha256": "72ada8c7d5c14cba0c77587315851d73b04342396823338245261e5a5983b2a3", "pdf": "reports/pdf/irreducibility-and-prime-ideals.pdf"}, {"id": "AG-05", "slug": "affine-morphisms-and-coordinate-rings", "title": "Affine Polynomial Maps and Coordinate-Ring Duality", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>The images of the coordinate functions determine the point map.\nRelations in the source coordinate ring guarantee that the reconstructed\npoint lies in the intended target.</p>", "target": "<p>For affine algebraic sets\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\subset k^n</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y\\subset k^m</annotation></semantics></math>,\npolynomial maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nare in bijection with unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphisms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nvia pullback\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*(h)=h\\circ F</annotation></semantics></math>.\nComposition is reversed. A polynomial map is an isomorphism with\npolynomial inverse if and only if its pullback is a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nisomorphism. Here polynomial maps mean maps whose coordinate functions\nare restrictions of polynomials.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use quotient rings, the vanishing ideal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\nof the actual point set, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I(X))=X</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor an algebraic set: if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=V(S)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\subset I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(I(X))\\subset X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile the reverse inclusion is definitional. Constants are fixed by a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nmap. No Nullstellensatz or algebraic closure is necessary for this\nformulation.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Define the pullback", "role": "<p>Compose representative polynomials and show the result is independent\nof representatives. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a well-defined unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphism.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=(F_1,\\ldots,F_m):X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a well-defined unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphism.</p>", "gate": "<p>Two representatives equal on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust remain equal after composition because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(X)\\subset Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If composition is defined before target membership is checked, verify\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(X)\\subset Y</annotation></semantics></math>;\notherwise relations in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nneed not vanish. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after\na versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For a polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\ncoordinates, substitute the polynomial coordinates of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain a polynomial function on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h-h&#39;\\in I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(h-h&#39;)(F(x))=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the resulting classes in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nagree.</p>", "<p>Composition preserves addition, multiplication, the constant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each scalar in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt also does not depend on the representatives chosen for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbecause those representatives agree pointwise on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the pullback assertion.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a well-defined unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphism.</p>", "Memory": "<p>A polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=(F_1,\\ldots,F_m):X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Compose representative polynomials and show the result is independent\nof representatives.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Two representatives equal on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust remain equal after composition because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(X)\\subset Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Reconstruct a map from coordinates", "role": "<p>Choose representatives for the images of coordinate classes and\nverify every defining relation of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong> There is a unique polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*=\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>There is a unique polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*=\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The images are elements of the quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso changing representatives must not change the point map.</p>", "repair": "<p>If arbitrary polynomial representatives are used without checking\nrelations, apply\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>\nto every relation in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nbefore claiming target membership. Withhold this export and recheck its\ndescendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar y_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the coordinate classes of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose polynomials\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresenting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi(\\bar y_j)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=(p_1(x),\\ldots,p_m(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRepresentatives differing by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive the same map.</p>", "<p>For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(\\bar y_1,\\ldots,\\bar y_m)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(p_1,\\ldots,p_m)\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)\\in V(I(Y))=Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn all coordinate classes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nagrees with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand these classes and constants generate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso agreement holds everywhere. The coordinate images also force\nuniqueness.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is a\nunique polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*=\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>A unital\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra\nhomomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi:k[Y]\\to k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Choose representatives for the images of coordinate classes and\nverify every defining relation of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The images are elements of the quotient\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso changing representatives must not change the point map.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Reverse composition and detect isomorphisms", "role": "<p>Compute compositions on functions and use uniqueness of the recovered\nmap. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> Pullback gives the stated\nbijection, reverses composition, and identifies polynomial isomorphisms\nwith algebra isomorphisms.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1; maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>F</mi></mover><mi>Y</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mover><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\xrightarrow{F}Y\\xrightarrow{G}Z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p>Pullback gives the stated bijection, reverses composition, and\nidentifies polynomial isomorphisms with algebra isomorphisms.</p>", "gate": "<p>The arrow directions reverse:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*=F^*\\circ G^*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If composition order is reversed incorrectly, evaluate both sides on\none function and rebuild the domain/codomain chain. Withhold this export\nand recheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For a function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Z</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*h=h\\circ G\\circ F=F^*(G^*h)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIdentity maps pull back to identity homomorphisms. E1 and E2 are inverse\nconstructions, giving the bijection.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas polynomial inverse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe composition identities show that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nare inverse. Conversely if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invertible, E2 realizes its inverse as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G:Y\\to X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth composite pullbacks are identities; uniqueness in E2 forces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G\\circ F=\\mathrm{id}_X</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\circ G=\\mathrm{id}_Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation: Pullback gives\nthe stated bijection, reverses composition, and identifies polynomial\nisomorphisms with algebra isomorphisms.</p>", "Memory": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1; maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>F</mi></mover><mi>Y</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mover><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\xrightarrow{F}Y\\xrightarrow{G}Z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N3.1, E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated\nassumptions and import versions.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Compute compositions on functions and use uniqueness of the recovered\nmap.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The arrow directions reverse:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*=F^*\\circ G^*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-3", "source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1; maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>F</mi></mover><mi>Y</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mover><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\xrightarrow{F}Y\\xrightarrow{G}Z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The arrow directions reverse:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*=F^*\\circ G^*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and E2/v1; maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>F</mi></mover><mi>Y</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mover><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\xrightarrow{F}Y\\xrightarrow{G}Z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The arrow directions reverse:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*=F^*\\circ G^*</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-define-the-pullback-1\">N1 — Define the pullback</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> For a polynomial\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\ncoordinates, substitute the polynomial coordinates of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain a polynomial function on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h-h&#39;\\in I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(h-h&#39;)(F(x))=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the resulting classes in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X]</annotation></semantics></math>\nagree.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Composition preserves addition,\nmultiplication, the constant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each scalar in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt also does not depend on the representatives chosen for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbecause those representatives agree pointwise on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the pullback assertion.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-reconstruct-a-map-from-coordinates-1\">N2 — Reconstruct a map\nfrom coordinates</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar y_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the coordinate classes of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose polynomials\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_j</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresenting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi(\\bar y_j)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=(p_1(x),\\ldots,p_m(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRepresentatives differing by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngive the same map.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\in I(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover><mi>y</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(\\bar y_1,\\ldots,\\bar y_m)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nApplying\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(p_1,\\ldots,p_m)\\in I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)\\in V(I(Y))=Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn all coordinate classes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nagrees with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand these classes and constants generate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso agreement holds everywhere. The coordinate images also force\nuniqueness.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-reverse-composition-and-detect-isomorphisms-1\">N3 — Reverse\ncomposition and detect isomorphisms</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> For a function\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\non\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Z</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G\\circ F)^*h=h\\circ G\\circ F=F^*(G^*h)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIdentity maps pull back to identity homomorphisms. E1 and E2 are inverse\nconstructions, giving the bijection.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas polynomial inverse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe composition identities show that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nare inverse. Conversely if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nis invertible, E2 realizes its inverse as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G^*</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor a polynomial map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G:Y\\to X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth composite pullbacks are identities; uniqueness in E2 forces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G\\circ F=\\mathrm{id}_X</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\circ G=\\mathrm{id}_Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\nfor the parabola\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y=V(y-x^2)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:\\mathbb A^1\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto(t,t^2)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ninduces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F^*:k[x,y]/(y-x^2)\\to k[t]</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\mapsto t</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\mapsto t^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts inverse sends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nto the class of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe corresponding geometric inverse is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x,y)\\mapsto x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBoth compositions are explicitly identities.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A pointwise bijective polynomial map need not be an isomorphism. Over\nan algebraically closed field of characteristic\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto t^p</annotation></semantics></math>\nis bijective: roots exist and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a-b)^p=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nforces equality. Its pullback\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[t]\\to k[t]</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\mapsto t^p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nis not surjective because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nis absent from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[t^p]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected final export:</strong> every bijective polynomial\nmap has a polynomial inverse. <strong>Sense witness:</strong> Frobenius\non the affine line in characteristic\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Ego promoted a set-theoretic property to an\nalgebraic one. <strong>Repair:</strong> use the actual criterion that\nthe pullback is an algebra isomorphism, as proved in N3. This rejects a\nstronger claim while preserving the exact §1 theorem; bijectivity alone\nremains insufficient.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Extend this affine viewpoint to gluing local\ncoordinate descriptions, while keeping regular maps and pointwise\nbijections distinct.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a href=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/ag.html\">J. S.\nMilne, Algebraic Geometry</a>, chapters on commutative algebra,\nalgebraic sets, and affine varieties; <a\nhref=\"https://www.jmilne.org/math/\">author’s mathematics site</a>.</p>", "sha256": "0ef6a681227563af115df96e311ea2aba2a90a1aa8244a478714d1b1495393ee", "pdf": "reports/pdf/affine-morphisms-and-coordinate-rings.pdf"}], "links": [{"source": "AG-02", "target": "AG-03", "label": "Weak Nullstellensatz", "detail": "AG-03 explicitly imports AG-02 under the version and assumptions in its import contract."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs relative to declared imports; no agent execution or formal verification claimed."};
